================================================================
  SMART WASTE COLLECTION SYSTEM  -  DHAKA CITY
  Sensor-driven route optimisation & capacity-aware scheduling
================================================================

--- 1. ROAD NETWORK --------------------------------------------
  Nodes : 5      Edges : 5
  Depot : Depot (node 0)
  Transfer stations : Transfer (node 3, cap 100.0 t/day)
  Landfills         : Landfill (node 4, cap 100.0 t/day)
  Unreachable nodes from depot : 0

--- 2. GREEDY URGENCY PRIORITISATION ---------------------------
  urgency = 100 * (0.60 * normalised_fill + 0.40 * normalised_age)

  Rank  Bin               Zone   Fill(t)  Age(h)   Urgency
  --------------------------------------------------------
  1     Bin_A                1      2.00    10.0     100.0
  2     Bin_B                1      1.50     5.0      65.0

--- 3. CAPACITY-AWARE SELECTION & ROUTING (per truck) ----------

  Truck Truck_1   (capacity 5.0 t, shift 200 min, start Depot)
    DP knapsack picked 2 bin(s)  ->  load 3.50 t / 5.00 t,   urgency value 165.0
        - Bin_A           2.00 t   urgency 100.0
        - Bin_B           1.50 t   urgency  65.0
    Route: Depot -> Bin_A -> Bin_B -> Transfer
      Depot          -> Bin_A             5.0 min   [Depot -> Bin_A]
      Bin_A          -> Bin_B             8.0 min   [Bin_A -> Transfer -> Bin_B]
      Bin_B          -> Transfer          4.0 min   [Bin_B -> Transfer]
    Travel 17.0 min + service 12.0 min = 29.0 min  (shift 200 min)  OK

--- 4. COLLECTION SUMMARY --------------------------------------
  Bins served          : 2 / 2
  Tonnage collected    : 3.50 t / 3.50 t
  Fleet capacity used  : 100.0 %

--- 5. MAX-FLOW / MIN-CUT ANALYSIS (Edmonds-Karp) -------------
  Flow network : 3 nodes, 2 edges
  Source       : Source
  Sink         : Landfill

  Edge capacities:
      Source       -> Transfer      10.00 t/day
      Transfer     -> Landfill       5.00 t/day

  Maximum feasible throughput : 5.00 t/day

  Minimum cut (bottleneck edges):
      Transfer     -> Landfill       5.00 t/day   <-- SATURATED

  The min-cut value equals the max-flow value (5.00 t/day): these edges are the
  infrastructure bottleneck that most constrains sustainable
  throughput and would govern any capacity-expansion decision.

================================================================
  Dijkstra chooses efficient paths.  Greedy prioritises urgent
  bins.  Dynamic programming respects truck capacity.  Max-flow
  exposes infrastructure bottlenecks.  One coordinated framework.
================================================================
